window.docContents[222].resolve({"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Extension/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___Extension-1-0":{"contents":"The canonical \\(Aron–Berner\\) extension\n\nFor z\\in X^{**} and a continuous (m+1)-linear form C on X, one step of the extension is the m-linear form\n(v_1,\\ldots,v_m)\\longmapsto z\\bigl(v\\mapsto C(v_1,\\ldots,v_m,v)\\bigr)\n(eq:partial). Iterating it n times extends the last variable first and gives \\overline A(z,\\ldots,z), the value at the diagonal point of the canonical extension (eq:arens, eq:AB). For a vector-valued polynomial the extension \\widetilde P\\colon X^{**}\\to Y^{**} is defined by \\widetilde P(z)(y^*)=\\widetilde{y^*\\circ P}(z) (eq:ABvector).\n\n\n","context":"","header":"LindenstraussPolynomials.Extension","id":"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Extension/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___Extension-1-0"}});